75 5.5 2.5 9.25 1.5 10.251 3.25 11.751 138.5 80.75 138.5 80.75L447 220.779s2.25-1.5 3-4.5 5.25-17 5-19.25zm-133.075 79.604l-.055-2.715 2.661 1.357-2.606 1.358zm74-43l-.055-2.715 2.661 1.358-2.606 1.357z"> </path> </g> </svg> <h4>STM32H7S</h4> </a> </div> </div> <div id="tab-4" class="inner-tab-content fade-in"> <p>The <a target="_blank" href="https://wiki.st.com/stm32mcu/wiki/Security:SBSFU_by_MCUboot#OEMiRoT_presentation">OEMiRoT</a>, based on MCUBoot technology, is an OEM solution delivered within the STM32Cube package. Like SBSFU, it enables secure boot and updates. Users can integrate and modify it as needed. By using WRP protections in combination with RDP, it can be made the first immutable boot stage.</p> <ul> <b>Features:</b> <li>Key for authentication/encryption stored in OBK storage when available</li> <li>Dual slot setup </li> <li>Full secure or secure/non-secure application supported (when TZ)</li> <li>Data slot can be used to store application updatable data</li> <li>Configuration and memory mapping define at compilation of OEMiRoT </li> </ul> <h3>Supported series</h3> <div class="card-grid"> <a target="_blank" href="https://www.st.com/en/microcontrollers-microprocessors/stm32h5-series.html" class="card"><svg viewBox="0 0 595.28 424.478" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"> <g fill="#03234b"> <path d="M192.822 178.105c9.109-5.266 19.117-10.658 28.08-15.84 4.682-2.706 9.712-5.137 13.68-8.16 1.994-1.518 2.565-3.551.803-5.64a264280.15 264280.15 0 0 0-63.944 37.109c.35.128.683.2 1.221.45 8.662.981 13.424-4.025 20.16-7.919z"> </path> <path d="M455 197.029c-.25-2.25-1.5-9.5-1.5-9.5s-.5-1.25-1.25-1.5a2.16 2.16 0 0 1-.146-.075v-7.115c-.74.424-22.884 13.104-26.202 15.2-3.375 2.133-11.724 6.484-16.52 2.133-4.796-4.352 1.243-7.195 1.243-7.195l23.28-13.422c-5.718-3.283-12.468-7.164-19.802-11.382v-7.334c-.74.424-22.884 13.104-26.202 15.2-3.375 2.133-11.724 6.484-16.52 2.133-4.796-4.352 1.243-7.195 1.243-7.195l23.152-13.349c-6.824-3.928-13.808-7.948-20.674-11.902v-6.8