real-time clock (RTC) in STM32 F0, F2, F3, F4 and L1 series of MCUs</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/7a/9c/de/da/84/e7/47/8a/DM00025071.pdf/files/DM00025071.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00025071.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN4992</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Overview secure firmware install (SFI)</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/group1/fb/aa/74/3f/a8/a9/49/a8/DM00355688/files/DM00355688.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00355688.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN5054</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Secure programming using STM32CubeProgrammer</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/group0/2a/fa/b5/dc/b4/52/46/47/DM00413494/files/DM00413494.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00413494.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN4838</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Managing memory protection unit (MPU) in STM32 MCUs</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/group0/bc/2d/f7/bd/fb/3f/48/47/DM00272912/files/DM00272912.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00272912.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN4246</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Proprietary Code Read Out Protection on STM32L1 microcontrollers</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/b4/14/62/81/18/57/48/05/DM00075930.pdf/files/DM00075930.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00075930.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN5421</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Getting started with STM32L5 Series microcontrollers and TrustZone<sup>®</sup> development</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/group1/90/2f/b6/c8/18/3e/41/27/DM00666290/files/DM00666290.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00666290.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN5347</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">STM32L5 Series TrustZone<sup>®</sup> features</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/group1/05/bb/91/81/a7/99/4e/ff/DM00625692/files/DM00625692.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00625692.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">AN5447</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Overview of Secure Boot and Secure Firmware Update solution on Arm<sup>®</sup> TrustZone<sup>®</sup></p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/application_note/group1/5f/8e/48/4c/1f/e1/41/0f/DM00684243/files/DM00684243.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00684243.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="hidden stm32-left">USER MANUAL</div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">UM2262</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Getting started with the X-CUBE-SBSFU STM32Cube Expansion Package</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/user_manual/group0/33/ee/5b/6b/c7/43/44/3e/DM00414687/files/DM00414687.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00414687.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">UM2237</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">STM32CubeProgrammer software description</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/user_manual/group0/76/3e/bd/0d/cf/4d/45/25/DM00403500/files/DM00403500.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00403500.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">UM2238</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">STM32 Trusted Package Creator tool software description </p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/resource/en/user_manual/dm00403513.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">UM2671</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Getting started with STM32CubeL5 TFM application</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/content/ccc/resource/technical/document/user_manual/group1/fb/57/0a/1c/6a/e1/44/fa/DM00678763/files/DM00678763.pdf/jcr:content/translations/en.DM00678763.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="hidden stm32-left">FLYERS</div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">STM32Trust</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">More Trust with STM32 - A whole security ecosystem around STM32</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/resource/en/flyer/flstm32trust.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="hidden stm32-left">PRESENTATIONS</div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">STM32H5 and Security FAQ</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Everything you need to know to implement security on STM32H5 MCUs</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/resource/en/product_presentation/faq-security-stm32h5.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">Fast-track your embedded security journey</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">Discover the STM32Trust TEE Secure Manager for STM32H5 MCUs</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/resource/en/product_presentation/secure-manager-introduction-v1.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-table__item"> <span class="st-table__cell-value">STM32Trust - an ecosystem for embedded security</span> <div class="st-table__col-list"> <div class="st-table__col-left"> <p class="st-copy">The STM32 security framework for protecting embedded systems</p> </div> <div class="st-table__col-right"> <a target="_blank" href="/resource/en/product_presentation/stm32trust-product-overview.pdf" class="st-link st-link--small st-link--uppercase st-link--underlined-blue" data-js="datasheetLink"> <svg class="st-link__icon st-link__icon"> <use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-download"></use> </svg> <span>PDF</span> </a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </form> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="openhtml"> <div class="modal" id="europe"> <div class="modal-content"> <button class="modal-close">&times;</button> <h2>Europe</h2> <p>In Europe, cybersecurity regulations for IoT and embedded devices are anchored by the <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng"><b>Cybersecurity Resilience Act (CRA)</b></a>, the <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A02014L0053-20241228"> <b>Radio Equipment Directive (RED)</b>. </a> <br>The CRA establishes a unified EU-wide cybersecurity framework to enhance the trustworthiness and resilience of digital products, including connected devices. The RED mandates essential requirements for radio equipment, which increasingly encompasses IoT devices, focusing on preventing vulnerabilities that could compromise user safety or privacy. </p> <ul>Please also visit our <a href="https://wiki.st.com/stm32mcu/wiki/Category:Security_regulations">STM32 MCU wiki pages on regulations</a> giving more descriptions and advise on how ST can help you with RED and CRA. <li> <a href="https://wiki.st.com/stm32mcu/wiki/Security:Deep_dive_on_RED"> Deep dive on RED </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://wiki.st.com/stm32mcu/wiki/Security:Q%26A_for_RED"> Q&A for RED </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://wiki.st.com/stm32mcu/wiki/Security:Deep_dive_on_CRA"> Deep dive on CRA </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://wiki.st.com/stm32mcu/wiki/Security:Q%26A_for_CRA"> Q&A for CRA </a> </li> </ul> <p>For further information, you can also watch the webinars part I and part II on the subject and download our detailed presentations and Q&A.</p> </div> </div> <div class="modal" id="united-states"> <div class="modal-content"> <button class="modal-close">&times;</button> <h2>United states</h2> <p>In the United States, regulatory and standardization efforts are led by bodies such as the <b>Federal Communications Commission (FCC)</b>, the <b>National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)</b>, and the U.S. <b>Food and Drug Administration (FDA)</b>, which develop and promote security requirements and guidelines applicable to various sectors, including medical products. These organizations work to safeguard IoT ecosystems, particularly in critical infrastructure, consumer applications, and governmental entities. Additionally, the <b>U.S. Cyber Trustmark</b> is a voluntary certification program that enables organizations to demonstrate their commitment to implementing cybersecurity best practices.</p> </div> </div> <div class="modal" id="china"> <div class="modal-content"> <button class="modal-close">&times;</button> <h2>China</h2> <p>China enforces strict cybersecurity requirements through the cybersecurity law and the <b>Multi-Level Protection Scheme (MLPS)</b>, which classifies devices according to security levels. Embedded devices with wireless functions must obtain <b>CCC certification</b>. Critical products undergo mandatory cybersecurity reviews by the <b>Cyberspace Administration of China (CAC)</b>. The <b>Personal Information Protection Law (PIPL)</b> sets stringent data management rules. Manufacturers must comply with national standards (GB standards) and work with accredited bodies, such as CCRC, for testing and certification.</p> </div> </div> <div class="modal" id="japan"> <div class="modal-content"> <button class="modal-close">&times;</button> <h2>Japan</h2> <p>Japan’s cybersecurity framework for embedded devices is primarily overseen by the <b>Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications (MIC)</b> and supported by the <b>National center of Incident readiness and Strategy for Cybersecurity (NISC)</b>. It focuses on ensuring the security, reliability, and safety of embedded systems used in critical infrastructure, telecommunications, and consumer electronics. Complementing this, <b>JC-STAR</b>, or <b>Japan cybersecurity Technical Assessment Requirements</b>, is a voluntary labeling scheme that assesses and visualizes the security of IoT products based on common standards. This helps consumers and businesses select devices with verified security levels to strengthen Japan’s digital infrastructure against cyberthreats.</p> </div> </div> <div class="modal" id="singapore"> <div class="modal-content"> <button class="modal-close">&times;</button> <h2>Singapore</h2> <p>Singapore’s cybersecurity framework for embedded devices is governed by the <b>Cybersecurity Act</b>, mandating licensing and compliance for critical systems. The <b>Cybersecurity Agency of Singapore (CSA)</b> issues guidelines promoting secure design, risk management, and incident response. The <b>Cybersecurity Labeling Scheme (CLS)</b> provides a voluntary labeling scheme to assess and communicate the security level of IoT and embedded devices, enhancing consumer trust. This integrated approach fosters collaboration between government, industry, and users to strengthen overall cybersecurity resilience.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="openhtml"> <script type="text/javascript" defer>
document.querySelectorAll(".js-st-micro.stmicro.cxv1 .st-container:not(.st-container--keep-padding) > .row > .large-12")
    .forEach(el => el.setAttribute("data-tabs-scope", "main"));

document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {

    // ─── TABS SCOPE INIT ───────────────────────────────────────────
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-tabs-scope]").forEach(scope => {
        scope.querySelector("[data-tabs]")?.hidden === false;
        scope.querySelectorAll("[data-tab-content]").forEach(c => c.hidden = true);
    });

    const overviewContent = document.querySelector('[data-tab-content="overview"]');
    const firstTrustTab   = document.querySelector('.st-trust-tab-item.first');
    if (overviewContent) overviewContent.hidden = false;
    if (firstTrustTab)   firstTrustTab.classList.add('active');

    // ─── FADE-IN OBSERVER ──────────────────────────────────────────
    const fadeObserver = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
        entries.forEach(entry => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                entry.target.classList.add("visible");
                fadeObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
        });
    }, { threshold: 0.2 });

    document.querySelectorAll(".fade-in").forEach(el => fadeObserver.observe(el));

    // ─── SWIPE HINT ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    document.querySelectorAll('.scroll-wrapper').forEach(wrapper => {
        const content = wrapper.querySelector('.map-wrap');
        const hint    = wrapper.querySelector('.swipe-hint');
        if (!content || !hint || !(content.scrollWidth > content.clientWidth)) return;

        hint.classList.add('visible');
        content.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
            if (content.scrollLeft > 10) hint.classList.remove('visible');
        }, { passive: true });
    });

    // ─── TRUST GRID MOSAIC CLICK ───────────────────────────────────
    document.querySelectorAll(".trust-grid-mosaic-box").forEach(box => {
        box.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const dataTab    = box.getAttribute('data-tab');
            const tabsWrap   = document.querySelector('.st-trust-tabs-wrap');
            const parToHide  = document.querySelector('.par-to-hide-for-inneractive');

            if (tabsWrap) {
                const top = tabsWrap.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - 200;
                window.scrollTo({ top, behavior: 'smooth' });
            }

            document.querySelectorAll(".st-trust-tab-item").forEach(t => t.classList.remove("active"));

            if (dataTab.includes('inner')) {
                parToHide?.classList.remove('active');
                document.querySelector('.st-tabs-tab[data-tab="security-functions-and-services"]')
                    ?.closest('li, [class*="tab-item"]')?.classList.add("active");
            } else {
                document.querySelector(`.st-tabs-tab[data-tab="${dataTab}"]`)
                    ?.closest('li, [class*="tab-item"]')?.classList.add("active");
                parToHide?.classList.add('active');
            }
        });
    });

    $(".inner-grid-mosaic .trust-grid-mosaic-box").on('click', function(){
        $(".inner-tabs .inner-st-trust-tab-item, .tabs-content .inner-tab-content").removeClass("active");
        $(".inner-tabs .inner-st-trust-tab-item:first-child, .tabs-content .inner-tab-content:first-child").addClass("active")
    })

    // ─── MULTIPLE FILES DOWNLOAD ───────────────────────────────────
    document.querySelector("#multiple-files-download-form-submit")
        ?.addEventListener('click', e => {
            e.preventDefault();
            document.getElementById('multiple-files-download-form')?.submit();
        });

});

// ─── DELEGATED CLICK: TAB NAVIGATION ──────────────────────────────
document.addEventListener("click", e => {

    // Trust tab items — active state
    const trustTab = e.target.closest('.st-trust-tab-item');
    if (trustTab) {
        document.querySelectorAll('.st-trust-tab-item').forEach(t => t.classList.remove('active'));
        trustTab.classList.add('active');

        const mosaicEl = document.querySelector('.trust-grid-mosaic');
        if (mosaicEl) mosaicEl.hidden = false;

        const firstInnerBtn = document.querySelector('.inner-tabs button');
        if (firstInnerBtn) firstInnerBtn.classList.remove('active');

        document.querySelectorAll('.inner-st-trust-tab-item, .inner-tab-content')
            .forEach((el, i) => { if (i === 0) el.classList.add('active'); });
    }

    // Scoped tab click
    const tab = e.target.closest("[data-tab]");
    if (tab) {
        const scope = tab.closest("[data-tabs-scope]");
        if (!scope) return;

        const target      = tab.dataset.tab;
        const tabsWrapper = scope.querySelector("[data-tabs]");
        const contents    = scope.querySelectorAll("[data-tab-content]");
        const content     = scope.querySelector(`[data-tab-content="${target}"]`);
        if (!content) return;

        if (tabsWrapper) tabsWrapper.hidden = true;
        contents.forEach(c => c.hidden = true);
        content.hidden = false;

        // Background image toggle on st-tabs-tab click
        const stTab = e.target.closest('.st-tabs-tab');
        const innerMosaicSR = e.target.closest('.trust-grid-mosaic-box[data-tab="standard-and-regulation"]')
        if (stTab) {
            const tabName     = stTab.dataset.tab;
            const parToHide   = document.querySelector('.par-to-hide-for-inneractive');
            const innerMosaic = document.querySelector('.inner-grid-mosaic');
            const bgEls       = document.querySelectorAll(
                '.js-st-micro.stmicro.cxv1 .st-container:not(.st-container--keep-padding) > .row > .large-12'
            );

            // Background image: remove on standard-and-regulation, restore otherwise
            bgEls.forEach(el => el.style.backgroundImage = tabName === 'standard-and-regulation' ? 'none' : '');

            // security-functions-and-services: show parToHide and inner-grid-mosaic
            if (tabName === 'security-functions-and-services') {
                parToHide?.classList.add('active');
                if (innerMosaic) innerMosaic.removeAttribute('hidden');
            }
        }

        if (innerMosaicSR) {
            const bgEls = document.querySelectorAll(
                '.js-st-micro.stmicro.cxv1 .st-container:not(.st-container--keep-padding) > .row > .large-12'
            );
            bgEls.forEach(el => el.style.backgroundImage = 'none');
        }
    }

    // Back button
    const back = e.target.closest(".tab-back");
    if (back) {
        const scope = back.closest("[data-tabs-scope]");
        if (!scope) return;

        const tabsWrapper = scope.querySelector("[data-tabs]");
        if (tabsWrapper) tabsWrapper.hidden = false;
        scope.querySelectorAll("[data-tab-content]").forEach(c => c.hidden = true);
        document.querySelector(".par-to-hide-for-inneractive")?.classList.add('active');
    }

    // Modal close
    if (e.target.classList.contains('modal-close') || e.target.classList.contains('modal')) {
        e.target.closest('.modal')?.classList.remove('is-open');
        document.querySelectorAll('circle').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('active'));
    }

});

// ─── INNER TABS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
document.querySelectorAll('.inner-st-trust-tab-item').forEach(tab => {
    tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
        document.querySelectorAll('.inner-st-trust-tab-item').forEach(t => t.classList.remove('active'));
        document.querySelectorAll('.inner-tab-content').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('active'));
        tab.classList.add('active');
        document.getElementById(tab.dataset.innertab)?.classList.add('active');
    });
});

// ─── MAP CIRCLES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
document.querySelector('.map-wrap')?.addEventListener('click', e => {
    const circle = e.target.closest('circle[data-country]');
    if (!circle) return;
    const modal = document.querySelector("#" + circle.dataset.country);
    if (!modal) return;
    circle.classList.add('active');
    modal.classList.add('is-open');
});

// ACTIVE TAB BASED ON HASH

document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  const hash = window.location.hash.slice(1); 
  if (!hash) return;

  const activeTab = document.querySelector(
    `#tabsScroll .st-tabs-tab[data-tab="${hash}"]`
  );
  if (!activeTab && hash !== "sesip") return;

  document.querySelectorAll(".st-trust-tab-item").forEach(el => el.classList.remove("active"));
  if(activeTab){
      activeTab.closest(".st-trust-tab-item")?.classList.add("active");
  }

  if(hash === "sesip"){
    document.querySelector(`.st-tabs-tab[data-tab="security-assurance-and-standards"]`)?.classList.add("active");
    document.querySelector(`.st-tabs-tab[data-tab="security-assurance-and-standards"]`).closest(".st-trust-tab-item")?.classList.add("active")
  }

  document.querySelectorAll(".section.tab-content").forEach(el => el.hidden = true);
  if(activeTab){
    const activeContent = document.querySelector(`.section.tab-content[data-tab-content="${hash}"]`);
    if (activeContent) activeContent.hidden = false;
  }

  if(hash === "sesip"){
    const activeContent = document.querySelector(`.section.tab-content[data-tab-content="security-assurance-and-standards"]`);
    if (activeContent) activeContent.hidden = false;
    setTimeout(() => {
        const sesipContent = document.querySelector(`[data-innertab="tab-41"]`)
        const sesipTopPosition = sesipContent.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - 150;

        window.scrollTo({ top: sesipTopPosition, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }, 1000)
  }
});

$(".trust-grid-mosaic.inner-grid-mosaic .trust-grid-mosaic-box").on('click', function(){
    $('.item-to-hide').hide();
})

$(".tab-back").on('click', function(){
    $('.item-to-hide').show();
})
</script> </div> <div class="newpar new section"> </div> <div class="par iparys_inherited"> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="st-container st-container--keep-padding"> <div class="row st-row"> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner--slider js-st-slider st-slider st-slider--content" data-slick='{&quot;autoplay&quot;: true, &quot;autoplaySpeed&quot;: 2000}'> <div> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner big-banner--yellow-bg lcb-border-pink "> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__icon"> </div> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__content"> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__content-text st-text-color--white"> <span>Protecting the data integrity and confidentiality on the <br/>STM32MP1 thanks to the power of STM32Trust</span> </div> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__content-button"> <a href="https://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/premium-content/premium-content-white-paper-protecting-oem-assets-and-ensuring-firmware-integrity-through-stm32-and-open-source-solutions.html" class="st-button st-button--primary" target="_blank" x-cq-linkchecker="skip"> <span>Discover more</span> <svg class="st-button__icon st-button__icon--right"> <use xlink:href="#icon-arrow-thin"></use> </svg> </a> </div> </div> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__poster lazyload" data-bg="/content/ccc/fragment/sales_and_marketing/banner/long_commercial_banner/group0/a4/b4/91/f5/68/1f/4d/d6/LCB_MP1xTrust_Image/files/LCB_MP1xTrust.jpg/jcr:content/translations/en.LCB_MP1xTrust.jpg"> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__poster-before big-banner--yellow-bg"></div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner big-banner--dark-bg lcb-border-pink "> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__icon"> </div> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__content"> <div class="st-long-commercial-banner__content-text st-text-color--white"> <span>Increase security and reduce complexity with STM32Trust TEE Secure Manager<br/>A set of turnkey services to simplify security development lifecycle